<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Radiology Information System (RIS)</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            A comprehensive imaging orchestration engine that manages the diagnostic pathway—from 
            order capture and technician worklists to finalized digital reporting and archival.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Imaging Order Orchestration</h2>
        <p>
            Streamline the diagnostic investigative process with digital order capture. Clinicians 
            can order a full range of imaging services—including X-Ray, Ultrasound, CT, 
            and MRI—directly from the consultation or ward dashboard. Orders are transmitted 
            instantly to the Radiology department, where technicians manage their daily 
            worklists through a prioritized interface, ensuring that emergency cases are 
            identified and handled with immediate priority.
        </p>
        <p>
            Standardized procedure coding ensures that imaging services are accurately 
            captured for clinical analytics and medical aid billing.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Technician Workflow & Reporting</h2>
        <p>
            Support your imaging professionals with a structured digital workspace. Technicians 
            document the successful completion of procedures, with the ability to 
            record critical clinical observations and technical details. Radiologists 
            utilize a specialized reporting module to generate digital results, 
            with integrated speech-to-text capabilities and standardized 
            templates optimized for rapid diagnostic turnaround.
        </p>
        <p>
            Finalized reports are automatically filed back into the patient's Electronic 
            Medical Record (EMR), making them immediately accessible to the 
            requesting doctor for review and clinical follow-up.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Diagnostic Archival & Quality</h2>
        <p>
            Maintain a permanent digital library of all imaging reports. The system provides 
            a searchable repository of every procedure performed, indexed by patient, 
            modality, and date. This archival focus enables long-term comparative studies 
            of a patient's diagnostic history, essential for managing chronic 
            conditions or post-operative recovery.
        </p>
        <p>
            Operational analytics visualize Radiology load and report turnaround times, 
            identifying bottlenecks and informing future equipment maintenance 
            and procurement cycles.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

